# pebble - my Time 2 dev environment
# Platform target for Pebble Time 2 = "emery". CLI installed via uv (own py3.13).
# Setup breadcrumb: ~/tries/2026-06-06-pebble/BREADCRUMB.md

# project lifecycle
pebble new-project myface              Create a new C project
pebble new-project --alloy myapp       Create a new pure-JavaScript (Alloy) project
pebble build                           Build .pbw for all platforms (run in project dir)
pebble clean                           Remove build artifacts

# emulator (QEMU) - emery = Time 2
pebble-shot                            BEST: build? no; install + screenshot + auto-kill emu (run in project dir)
pebble-shot -b                         build first, then install + screenshot + auto-kill
pebble-shot -k                         keep emulator running afterward (don't auto-kill)
pebble-shot -p emery -o out.png        pick platform / output path
# pebble-shot lives in ~/dotfiles/scripts/.local/bin/ (stowed). Handles the flaky
# cold-boot install (retries warm) and ALWAYS tears down the emulator so no
# leftover/zombie QEMU windows pile up.
pebble install --emulator emery        Boot emulator + install app (reuses running emu)
pebble screenshot --emulator emery out.png   Capture emulator screen to PNG
pebble logs --emulator emery           Stream app logs from emulator
pebble kill                            Stop ALL running emulators (closes the QEMU window)
kill $(pgrep qemu-pebble)              Safe manual kill (do NOT pkill -f qemu-pebble: self-matches)

# physical watch (over Bluetooth via companion app)
pebble install --phone <ip>            Install to watch via phone on same network
pebble logs --phone <ip>               Stream logs from physical watch

# SDK management
pebble sdk install latest              Install latest SDK
pebble sdk list                        List installed + available SDKs
pebble --version                       Show tool + active SDK version

# install / update the tool itself (uv-managed, pinned to py3.13)
uv tool install pebble-tool --python 3.13     Install (system py3.14 is too new)
uv tool upgrade pebble-tool                    Upgrade the CLI

# platform codenames
aplite     Pebble Classic / Steel (144x168 b&w)
basalt     Pebble Time / Time Steel (color)
chalk      Pebble Time Round
diorite    Pebble 2
flint      Pebble 2 Duo
emery      Pebble Time 2   <-- my watch
gabbro     Pebble Round 2

